/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 50 750 Tm (ACME Corporation - Global Security & Authentication Policy \(v2.4\)) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 722 Tm (1. Purpose and Scope) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 708 Tm (This document outlines the mandatory authentication, access control, and identity management rules for all employees, contractors, and automated services accessing ACME corporate assets and databases.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 680 Tm (2. Authentication Policy) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 666 Tm (- Multi-Factor Authentication \(MFA\): All user and administrative access to internal services, email, cloud infrastructure, and databases requires mandatory Multi-Factor Authentication \(MFA\) using FIDO2 hardware keys or approved mobile authenticator applications. SMS-based 2FA is explicitly forbidden due to SIM-swapping vulnerabilities.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 652 Tm (- Password Standards: Passwords must be at least 16 characters in length and comprise uppercase letters, lowercase letters, numbers, and symbols. Passwords must not be reused across corporate and personal accounts.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 638 Tm (- Password Expiration: Master credentials must be rotated every 90 days. Reusing any of the last 10 passwords is blocked by directory services.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 624 Tm (- Account Lockout: System accounts are locked out automatically after 5 consecutive failed authentication attempts. A security alert is generated to the Security Operations Center \(SOC\).) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 610 Tm (- Session Duration and Inactivity: Active web sessions and CLI credentials automatically expire after 15 minutes of inactivity, requiring re-authentication.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 582 Tm (3. Remote Access & Network Security) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 568 Tm (- All remote access must originate from corporate-managed endpoints and pass through the corporate Zero-Trust Network Access \(ZTNA\) gateway.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 554 Tm (- Public Wi-Fi access requires active VPN tunneling at all times.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 540 Tm (- Split-tunneling is disabled on all corporate devices.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 512 Tm (4. Incident Reporting & Violations) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 498 Tm (Any suspected credential compromise or unauthorized access attempt must be reported immediately to security@acmecorp.internal within 1 hour of discovery.) Tj
ET

